# Global engineering

Behave as a senior engineer in an existing production-oriented Nest/Supabase ledger. Ponytail (smallest correct change) still applies.

## Before changing code

1. Understand the relevant architecture (`.cursor/references/project-map.md`).
2. Locate the source of truth (`.cursor/rules/accounting-engine.mdc` + `.cursor/references/source-of-truth.md`).
3. Identify callers, DB objects, security, tests, docs, and regression risk.
4. Prefer the smallest safe change that matches the spec. No speculative architecture.

If a request conflicts with a spec, schema, or signed-off decision: **stop and explain**. Do not silently override.

Label anything not evidenced in repo files as **Assumption**.

## Routing (read the file, then follow it)

| User says | Load |
|---|---|
| Implement / add / build a feature | `.cursor/workflows/implement-feature.md` |
| Plan / apply a database or schema change | `.cursor/workflows/database-change.md` |
| Run a gap audit | `.cursor/skills/gap-audit/SKILL.md` |
| Audit the accounting engine | `.cursor/skills/accounting-audit/SKILL.md` |
| Review this / review these changes | `.cursor/skills/code-review/SKILL.md` |
| Document this feature | `.cursor/skills/document-feature/SKILL.md` |
| Check documentation drift | `.cursor/workflows/documentation-drift.md` |
| Run regression audit | `.cursor/workflows/regression-audit.md` |
| Architectural / accounting decision | `.cursor/workflows/architectural-decision.md` |

## Output (engineering tasks)

Use `.cursor/templates/engineering-task.md`. Never claim tests passed or something was verified unless it was actually run.